A||||8||GT Bastard||A note to those changing V6 alternators...||||14||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||04-19-2000||08:58 PM||||I tried changing my alternator a per the Chiltons instructions, and it sucks!  It's all good until you get to "disconnecting the tie rod end"  to provide clearance.  After fighting with the idea, I decided it was going to be absolutely necessary to do this (although I've heard it's not necessary on manual cars...)  Anyhow, It's a pain in the arse to disconnect the tie rod.  <P>Instead....<BR>Remove that silly aluminum tube that cools the back of your alternator.  Disconnect the #1 spart plug wire(the aluminum boot is in the way.)  Then remove the alternator bracket(3 bolts.)  Now you can just BARELY squeeze the alternator through the top!  If you're standing behind your car, it'll come out just to the left of the doggy bone.  When I finally got it out, I was so happy I screamed f*** yeah b*tch!  <P>ps... Advanced auto had the best price.  The high output 94 amp alternator was 67 bucks.  It's a Delco Remy. ||||reg||14
Z||000001||bHooper||04-20-2000||01:19 PM||||Well actually, Bastard, I have found that Advance has one available for $60 (after $40 core) with a 1 year waranty.  The one you mentioned is the "lifetime" unit for $67.49.<P>Autozone has one for $69.95+$30 core and NAPA's is $72.99+$27 core.<P>The "lifetime waranty" thing makes me wonder how many of those I have had on variouse parts, considering that I have owned my car for 11 years  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I should be making money on those deals anytime soon.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||04-20-2000||02:28 PM||||Damn, the Napa here said they wanted 100 bucks! That's assuming you give them your old one.  They told me they had to order it as well.  The 60 dollar unit here at Advanced was the lower output model(without a/c.)  Crazy.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gold-86SE||04-20-2000||04:36 PM||||I had to replace my alternator about a month ago, while on the road to my in-laws.<P>Bought mine at Auto Zone, ruffly a hundred bucks, but they were the closest at the time. But I am figuring out the Advance Auto Parts is a little cheaper.<P>Anyway, here is how I changed my alternator, my Fiero is V6 4spd.<P>I just pulled off the neg. bat. cable, unbolted the alternator, lowered in to the ground (diagonally between the exhaust header and trunk wall), crawled under the car disconneted the wires, and bam it was done.<BR>A simple 15 minute job, with high hopes of easy re-entry and hookup, but boy was I wrong.<P>I put the alternator back in the way I brought it out.  I connected the wires under the car, and lifted the alternator back up into posistion.<P>Getting it bolted back together, that was the witchy part.  I finally got smart and removed the stupid air tube to the alternator to allowing hand access to replace the top bolt. Bolting it back together took 3x as long as dropping it.<P>All this was done under a street lamp, no-less, and finally completed with the aide of my lovely and gracious wife who came to my rescue.<p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 04-20-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000004||GT Bastard||04-20-2000||06:35 PM||||I wish mine were that easy... There's no way I coulda dropped mine though the bottom like that.  I actually thought installing it was much easier...  I wonder what's different.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||04-20-2000||09:19 PM||||we had to jack my car up really high so that the strut was fully extended, then the alternator dropped through the bottom with a lot of work.  My formula doesnt have the metal pipe like my 86GT has.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gokart||04-20-2000||09:29 PM||||Mine was as easy as Gold-86SE's on my 87GT. I loosened the original one to pull it back with a long crow bar to tighten a sqeeky belt and I broke the the part with the bolt right off <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> Replaced it with the one from my parts car in about 20 minutes! Just fell right out after loosening it from bracket.||||reg||14
Z||000007||TheFiero64||04-21-2000||06:20 PM||||I hope mine is easy too! I need to replace it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000008||Ozzy||04-21-2000||09:43 PM||||I assume it is the auto tranny creating the problem. I dropped mine out the bottom. Removed the old and installed the new in about Lenscrafters!(in about an hour  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
